{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization retaining the upper representation bounds and the conditional consequence of Duke–Schulze-Pillot (Invent. Math. 99, 1990), and adding an unconditional fixed-cap theorem for x^2+y^2+z^2. H1: for every unit vector u in R^3 and every epsilon > 0 there is T such that every squarefree t >= T with t congruent to 3 modulo 8 has an integer representation x with sum x_i^2=t and |x_i-sqrt(t)u_i| <= epsilon sqrt(t) for every coordinate. The new statement takes no analytic estimate as a hypothesis. Its proof combines finite-degree harmonic Weyl bounds, odd-degree cancellation, a positive minimum of finitely many degree-dependent savings, and a representation lower bound supplied by the verified Siegel theorem. The threshold is ineffective. The original three unconditional upper/divisor bounds and two conditional statements are retained unchanged; the latter still require hThm1 and hThm3i for general ternary forms. No unconditional general Duke–Schulze-Pillot theorem, sharp 1/175 exponent, spinor-genus lower bound or numerical cutoff is claimed.",
